{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Infra.BorelRank","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.NumberField.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.NumberField.Embeddings"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.cyclotomicBorelRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.cyclotomicBorelRank","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L69-L77","doc":"Cyclotomic field embeddings: for `ℚ(ζ_K)` with `K` prime `≥ 3`,\n`(r_1, r_2) = (0, (K-1)/2)`.  Borel rank at depth `n`:\n\n  n even: `(K-1)/2`\n  n odd:  `(K-1)/2`\n\n(same formula in this case since `r_1 = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.rank_formula_arith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.rank_formula_arith","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Verified arithmetic: the predicted rank at depth `n` is\ndetermined by parity of `n` and the embedding pair\n`(r_1, r_2)`.  This is the closed-form Borel formula\nstripped of K-theoretic content — pure case-split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.rank_witness_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.rank_witness_2","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L60-L60","doc":"At depth `2` (Bloch-Suslin), the witness is discharged.\nThis is the canonical \"depth-2 unconditional\" content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.rank_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.rank_witness","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L57-L57","doc":"At depth `n`, the predicted Borel rank agrees with the\nactual `dim_ℚ K_{2n-1}^{ind}(F) ⊗ ℚ`.  Stated as an\nopaque predicate that concrete instances may discharge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.r2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.r2","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Number of pairs of complex embeddings of `F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.r1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.r1","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Number of real embeddings of `F`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.BorelRank","kind":"class","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L34-L67","doc":"**Borel rank as a class.**  Records the rank of the\nindecomposable K-theory at every depth `n ≥ 2` for the\nrelevant field.  Concrete instances (e.g. cyclotomic fields\n`ℚ(ζ_K)`) instantiate `(r_1, r_2)` and supply a\n`rank_witness` predicate identifying `borelRankPredicted` with\nthe actual `dim_ℚ K_{2n-1}^{ind}(F) ⊗ ℚ`.\n\nPer Gemini review: the previous existence-only field\n`∃ d, d = borelRankPredicted n r1 r2` was vacuous (always\nsatisfiable by `⟨borelRankPredicted n r1 r2, rfl⟩`).  Mirrors\nthe meaningful pattern used in `QOU.Infra.Polylogarithm.TheoremA`:\na `rank_witness : ℕ → Prop` predicate that concrete instances\nsharpen plus a verified arithmetic identity at depth `2`\n(where Bloch-Suslin discharges unconditionally) and `3`\n(where the rank formula reduces to elementary arithmetic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Infra.BorelRank.borelRankPredicted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Infra.BorelRank.borelRankPredicted","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Infra/BorelRank.lean#L24-L32","doc":"Borel rank of `K_{2n-1}^{ind}(F) ⊗ ℚ` for a number field with\n`(r_1, r_2)` real-and-complex embeddings.  For `n ≥ 2`:\n\n  n even: `r_1 + r_2`\n  n odd:  `r_2`\n\nFormula expressed on naturals. ","signatureChunk":0}]}